# Inspect logs for failed tests

The output of each test build goes to its own `build.log` file, which keeps the main build output readable. When a test fails on a CI system, though, the files of the build workspace are often hard to reach.

Set the `streamLogsOnFailures` parameter of the [`run`](../run-mojo.html#streamLogsOnFailures) or [`verify`](../verify-mojo.html#streamLogsOnFailures) goal to print the `build.log` of every failed test to the main build output once all tests have finished.

```xml
<project>
  ...
  <build>
    <plugins>
      <plugin>
        <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
        <artifactId>maven-invoker-plugin</artifactId>
        <version>${project.version}</version>
        <configuration>
          <streamLogsOnFailures>true</streamLogsOnFailures>
        </configuration>
      </plugin>
    </plugins>
  </build>
  ...
</project>
```
